{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SAVE BUTTON (HEART)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Heart that adds a product to the visitor's saved items (behaviour in assets/saved-books.js). Works for every product
except gift cards (the eGift card, and the physical ones, which are a normal product of type "Physical Gift Cards").
The names (save-book-button, saved-books) are kept from when only audiobooks could be saved, so existing lists, links
and the account metafield keep working.

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* product: the product to save
* size: the icon size in pixels (default 24)
* overlay: if true, the heart sits in a round white button over the corner of the card image (the parent must be
  positioned)
* class: optional extra classes
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- unless product.gift_card? or product.type contains 'Gift Card' -%}
  {%- assign icon_size = size | default: 24 -%}

  <save-book-button class="save-book {% if overlay %}save-book--overlay{% endif %} {{ class }}" product-id="{{ product.id }}" product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}" product-type="{{ product.type | escape }}">
    <button type="button" class="save-book__button tap-area" aria-pressed="false" aria-label="Save {{ product.title | escape }}">
      {%- render 'icon' with 'picto-love', width: icon_size, height: icon_size -%}
    </button>
  </save-book-button>
{%- endunless -%}
